# Kestrel secrets / environment — Pi deployment
#
# Copy this file to the real one and fill it in:
#
#   cp deploy/kestrel.env.example ~/.config/kestrel/kestrel.env
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/kestrel/kestrel.env
#
# The real file is NEVER committed to git, never copied into a backup
# destination, and never leaves the Pi except into a password manager for
# disaster recovery. Both systemd units load it via `EnvironmentFile=`
# (see deploy/systemd/*.service) — the process environment is the only place
# these values live.
#
# Every variable below is read by the code today (grepped for `os.environ`/
# `getenv` across agent/ and server/ - nothing here is reserved/aspirational).
# Everything is optional unless said otherwise: leaving a whole section unset
# means the matching capability is off, and Kestrel logs that and falls back
# rather than failing to start (fake board, fake mail reader, no brain, no
# GitHub landing/validation). Keep unused variables commented out rather than
# set to empty strings, so a stray blank secret can't be mistaken for
# "configured".

# --- Core --------------------------------------------------------------------

# Root of all durable state: kestrel.db, the session-host socket, the auth
# token file, the memory git repo, and (if brain_work_dir is ever inspected)
# the brain's scratch dir. The session host AND the server must be given the
# SAME value - both default to ~/.kestrel if this is unset, which is enough
# on a single-account Pi, but set it explicitly here so the two units can
# never drift apart.
KESTREL_DATA=/home/callum028/.kestrel

# Where the server itself listens - used both as the default the server binds
# to conceptually and as the URL hooks/kestrel-wait/the brain's MCP server
# call back into. Only needs overriding if you move it off the default port
# (also update deploy/systemd/kestrel-server.service's --port and
# web/src/api.ts's FALLBACK_API together).
# KESTREL_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8099

# Extra origins the browser's Origin header is allowed to send from, on top
# of the built-in dev/Tauri set (localhost:5173, tauri://localhost, ...) -
# see docs/design.md §11a and deploy/README.md's "Tailscale Serve" section.
# This is what lets the web app work when it's opened at the HTTPS tailnet
# URL `tailscale serve` fronts, rather than every request 403ing. Always
# additive, comma-separated if more than one, never a way to disable the
# check itself.
# KESTREL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://kestrel-pi.tailXXXX.ts.net

# Where the built web app (`web/dist`, from `npm run build` - deploy.sh does
# this automatically) is served from at `/` - see server/kestrel/web_static.py.
# Defaults to <this checkout>/web/dist, which is already correct for a normal
# deploy.sh release layout. Only set this if you build the frontend somewhere
# else, or want to point at a different build without redeploying.
# KESTREL_WEB_DIST=/home/callum028/kestrel/current/web/dist

# The one-time pairing link a device needs to get the API token without it
# ever being baked into the bundle - see `kestrel-pair` / `python -m
# kestrel.pair` and deploy/README.md. Not read by the server itself, only by
# that command - it has no other way to know the tailnet's own HTTPS address.
# KESTREL_PUBLIC_URL=https://kestrel-pi.tailXXXX.ts.net

# --- Claude Code executor / projects ------------------------------------------

# Which repos a task's worktree may be created in: "name=path" pairs,
# comma-separated - not JSON, so it stays one line here. `name` is also the
# key used by KESTREL_VALIDATION_<NAME>_* below and (if there's more than
# one project) the `scope` a task must set to disambiguate which repo it
# belongs to.
# KESTREL_CLAUDE_PROJECTS=kestrel=/home/callum028/workspace/github/kestrel

# Where per-task worktrees are created. Defaults to $KESTREL_DATA/worktrees.
# KESTREL_WORKTREES_ROOT=/home/callum028/.kestrel/worktrees

# The `claude` binary the executor launches interactive sessions with.
# Defaults to "claude" (resolved on PATH).
# KESTREL_CLAUDE_BINARY=claude

# --- Validation, per project (design §5 step 7) -------------------------------
# <NAME> is the same project name used in KESTREL_CLAUDE_PROJECTS, upper-cased
# (e.g. the "kestrel" project's variables are all KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_*).
# A project with none of these set gets the explicit "no validation
# configured — merged and deployed, not tested" pass-through, not an error.
# Repeat the whole block once per project that needs validation.

# GitHub Actions workflow file name to confirm the merge commit deployed
# (checked via the GitHub API - needs GITHUB_TOKEN/GH_TOKEN below).
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_DEPLOY_WORKFLOW=deploy.yml
# A URL to poll instead of, or in addition to, the workflow - "ready" once it
# returns 200 (and matches DEPLOY_URL_MATCH, if given).
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_DEPLOY_URL=https://dev.kestrel.internal/health
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_DEPLOY_URL_MATCH=
# How long to wait for the deploy to confirm before treating it as failed.
# Default 15 minutes.
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_DEPLOY_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=15
# The authoritative test command Kestrel itself runs against dev once
# deployed - no command means no test run, deploy confirmation is all that
# happens.
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_COMMAND=npx playwright test
# Where that command writes its report (relative to the project). Default
# "report.json".
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_REPORT_PATH=report.json
# How long the command may run before it's treated as a failure. Default 20
# minutes.
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=20
# The dev URL to pass through to the validation command (e.g. as an env var
# Playwright's own config reads) - not fetched by Kestrel itself.
# KESTREL_VALIDATION_KESTREL_DEV_URL=https://dev.kestrel.internal

# --- GitHub --------------------------------------------------------------------
# PR discovery, CI status for waits, and merge-on-green (design §5 step 6).
# Unset means no landing/validation gate runs at all - tasks stay in RUNNING.

# A personal access token with repo scope. GH_TOKEN is checked as a fallback
# if this is unset (same variable `gh auth token` already populates, so a box
# with `gh auth login` already done needs nothing extra here).
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GH_TOKEN=
# "owner/name" of the repo PRs land in.
# KESTREL_GITHUB_REPO=callum028/kestrel

# --- Notion (board sync) -------------------------------------------------------
# Unset means an in-memory fake board - nothing written reaches Notion.

# KESTREL_NOTION_TOKEN=
# KESTREL_NOTION_DATABASE_ID=
# Everything below has a sane default matching Callum's own board and only
# needs setting if a property is named differently.
# KESTREL_NOTION_API_VERSION=2022-06-28
# KESTREL_NOTION_POLL_SECONDS=60
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_TITLE=Name
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_BODY=Description
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_STATUS=Status
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_FLAG=Kestrel flag
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_PR=PR
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_HANDLE=ID
# KESTREL_NOTION_PROPERTY_PROJECT=Project

# --- Mail (Microsoft Graph, read-only) -----------------------------------------
# Unset means FakeMailReader - Kestrel still starts, just against placeholder
# mail. Both come from an Entra ID app registration (see README.md's "Mail
# (Microsoft Graph)" section for the one-time setup and the device-code sign-in
# via `kestrel-mail-auth`, which stores the refresh token at
# $KESTREL_DATA/mail_token - not itself an environment variable).

# KESTREL_MAIL_TENANT_ID=
# KESTREL_MAIL_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Brain (headless `claude -p` behind Kestrel's own conversation) -----------
# Unset KESTREL_BRAIN_CLAUDE_BINARY means the brain is off entirely: no
# conversational replies beyond the stub responder, and every delivery falls
# back to its fixed deterministic template rather than being reworded.

# The `claude` binary the brain's headless calls use. Setting this is what
# turns the brain on - there is no separate on/off switch.
# KESTREL_BRAIN_CLAUDE_BINARY=claude
# Extra arguments passed to every headless `claude -p` call, before the
# flags brain/runner.py itself adds (--print, --model, ...). Shell-style
# splitting, so quote a value that contains spaces the way you would in a
# systemd ExecStart line. Rarely needed - most deployments leave this unset.
# KESTREL_BRAIN_BASE_ARGS=
# How long a single headless call may run before it's treated as failed.
# Default 60 seconds.
# KESTREL_BRAIN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# The `--model` alias/name passed to the CLI for the two tiers
# brain/routing.py's decide_model picks between (Haiku by default, Sonnet for
# turns that ask for depth or a finished-task summary - see that module).
# Defaults match the CLI's own built-in aliases; set these instead if you
# want to pin an exact model rather than let the CLI resolve the alias.
# KESTREL_BRAIN_HAIKU_MODEL=haiku
# KESTREL_BRAIN_SONNET_MODEL=sonnet
# The command the brain's `claude -p` calls launch its MCP server with
# (kestrel-mcp, server/kestrel/brain/mcp_server.py) - by default the same
# Python interpreter running the server process, invoking
# `python -m kestrel.brain.mcp_server`, which needs no PATH entry and is
# almost always correct once `-e server` is installed into that venv. Only
# set this to point at the installed `kestrel-mcp` console script directly
# (e.g. on a packaged/production layout where the brain's `claude` subprocess
# doesn't inherit the server's own venv on its PATH):
# KESTREL_BRAIN_MCP_COMMAND=/home/callum028/kestrel/current/venv/bin/kestrel-mcp
# Extra arguments for that MCP server command - shell-style splitting, same
# as KESTREL_BRAIN_BASE_ARGS above. Only relevant alongside
# KESTREL_BRAIN_MCP_COMMAND; the default invocation (`-m
# kestrel.brain.mcp_server`) is set in code, not overridable through this.
# KESTREL_BRAIN_MCP_ARGS=

# --- Push notifications (Web Push / VAPID) -------------------------------------
# No environment variables: the VAPID keypair is generated once on first run
# and stored 0600 at $KESTREL_DATA/vapid_private_key.pem. Nothing to
# configure here.

# --- Read by deploy/backup.sh and deploy/deploy.sh (shell scripts, not the
# --- app itself - grepped for "${VAR" in deploy/*.sh) --------------------------

# Private git remote(s) the nightly backup pushes to. Use SSH remotes
# (git@github.com:you/kestrel-backups.git) so no token needs to sit in this
# file just to push - the Pi's own deploy key/SSH config handles auth. The
# SQLite backup and the memory repo can share one remote (different branches)
# or use two - MEMORY_BACKUP_REMOTE falls back to BACKUP_REMOTE if unset.
# Required for deploy/backup.sh to run at all.
# BACKUP_REMOTE=git@github.com:callum028/kestrel-backups.git
# MEMORY_BACKUP_REMOTE=

# Overrides for deploy.sh's own layout/health-check assumptions - only worth
# setting if you deviate from the standard ~/kestrel layout or port 8099.
# KESTREL_HOME=/home/callum028/kestrel
# KESTREL_HEALTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8099/health

# --- Set automatically, not by you ---------------------------------------------
# KESTREL_TASK_ID is set per-session by the Claude Code executor (not read
# from this file) so kestrel-hook/kestrel-wait, invoked from inside a task's
# worktree, know which task they're attributing themselves to. Never set it
# here.
